---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 3em 1em;
			}
			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			p {
				line-height: 1.6;
				color: var(--gray-dark, #333);
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
			}
			ul {
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
				padding-left: 1.25em;
			}
			li {
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About ResizeForge</h1>
			<p>
				<strong>ResizeForge</strong> is a high-speed, privacy-first web utility built to make image resizing, compression, and format conversion effortless for creators, developers, designers, and everyday web users.
			</p>

			<h2>Our Mission</h2>
			<p>
				Most traditional online image converters require users to upload their personal photos and graphics to remote cloud servers. This introduces unnecessary privacy risks, slow upload queues, bandwidth consumption, and server storage delays.
			</p>
			<p>
				ResizeForge was created with a simple philosophy: <em>your files belong to you</em>. By leveraging modern client-side browser technologies, all processing happens locally on your device without transmitting your image data over the network.
			</p>

			<h2>How It Works</h2>
			<p>
				ResizeForge utilizes the modern <strong>HTML5 Canvas API</strong> and the browser's native rendering engine to compute pixel transformations directly inside your web browser. 
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>100% In-Browser Execution:</strong> When you drop an image into ResizeForge, JavaScript loads the binary data into your local browser memory.</li>
				<li><strong>Zero Server Uploads:</strong> No image files are ever uploaded, saved, cached, or seen by our servers or any third parties.</li>
				<li><strong>Hardware Accelerated:</strong> Rendering and scaling are accelerated by your device's GPU and CPU, providing near-instantaneous output even for large high-resolution images.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Key Features</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Custom Pixel Dimensions:</strong> Enter precise width and height values for any custom layout requirement.</li>
				<li><strong>Aspect Ratio Lock:</strong> Automatically calculate proportional dimensions to eliminate image stretching or distortion.</li>
				<li><strong>Smart Scale Presets:</strong> Scale down or up by standard percentages (25%, 50%, 75%, 100%, 150%, 200%) in a single click.</li>
				<li><strong>Do Not Enlarge Protection:</strong> Safeguard image sharpness by preventing accidental upscaling beyond native resolution.</li>
				<li><strong>Multi-Format Conversion:</strong> Export your output as high-fidelity PNG, compressed JPEG, or modern WebP format with granular quality control.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Free & Ad-Supported</h2>
			<p>
				ResizeForge is completely free to use with no hidden subscriptions, no daily usage limits, and no watermark additions. To maintain our infrastructure and keep our tools free and accessible for everyone worldwide, we support our platform through non-intrusive digital advertisements.
			</p>

			<h2>Get in Touch</h2>
			<p>
				We are constantly refining our tools to support more formats and workflow features. If you have suggestions, feature requests, or questions, please visit our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> or email us directly at <a href="mailto:support@resizeforge.online">support@resizeforge.online</a>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

